    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="0702" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7289</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. T. K. Bewley, of the British Supply Council in North
                        America, to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-02">August 2, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Dean</hi>: This is to let you know that my
                    government has now proposed to the Chinese Government the appointment of Mr.
                    Hall Patch<anchor n="46" xml:id="d727-f1"/> as British member of the
                    Stabilisation Board and that this proposal has been accepted by the Chinese
                    Government.</p>
                <p>The appointment would be on a temporary basis and the more permanent appointment
                    would no doubt be the subject of discussion with Sir O. E. Niemeyer.</p>
                <p>I have also informed Mr. Cochran<anchor n="47" xml:id="d727-f2"/> of the
                    appointment.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>T. K. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bewley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d727-f1" n="46" xml:id="d727-f1-content">
                <p>Financial Adviser of the British Embassy in China until 1939.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d727-f2" n="47" xml:id="d727-f2-content">
                <p>H. Merle Cochran, Technical Assistant to the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
